    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0265" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg159"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan telegraphs that the revolutionists were entirely successful in a
                    decisive battle fought at Valparaiso on the 28th of August; that Balmaceda
                    resigned the next day, and that the revolutionists were now fully installed. He
                    asks whether he can recognize the new Government, and states that everything is
                    tranquil.</p>
            </div>
